{
  "code_scheme": "LAU",
  "description": "The 100 Luxembourg communes in force since 1 September 2023, keyed by their LAU 2 code. `members` is empty on purpose: the gazetteer is produced by the pipeline from an authoritative source and published as an artifact, not hand-maintained here.\n`valid_from` is the producer's own effective date, not an assumption. STATEC's LAU code register (A1106.xlsx, sheet \"LU_SEP 2023\") states it verbatim as \"codes UAL au 01.09.2023 (100 communes)\". It is corroborated by the two acts that produced the current set, both of which say in their Article 13 \"La présente loi entre en vigueur le 1er septembre 2023\":\n  - Loi du 3 mars 2023 portant fusion des communes de Grosbous et de Wahl,\n    creating « Groussbus-Wal » (LAU 0711)\n    https://legilux.public.lu/eli/etat/leg/loi/2023/03/03/a115/jo\n  - Loi du 3 mars 2023 portant fusion des communes de Bous et de Waldbredimus,\n    creating « Bous-Waldbredimus » (LAU 1209)\n    https://legilux.public.lu/eli/etat/leg/loi/2023/03/03/a117/jo\n\nThe code space is the national LAU scheme: two digits of canton (LAU 1) plus two of commune, zero-padded. The codes carried by the statec-lustat dataflow were checked on 2026-08-19 to be exactly the 100 codes in STATEC's LAU register, so statistical series join to this set on code without a crosswalk.\nCommune boundary *geometry* is deliberately absent. This set declares the code space only; choosing a geometry producer is a separate decision recorded in docs/adr/0007-commune-geography-authority.md.",
